  "security_implications": "Chunk configures error and fault status registers capturing integrity violations (regfile_intg, shadow, ctrl_fsm_intg, key_ecc, etc.). Incorrect setting or clearing of these bits could mask critical hardware failures, potentially allowing corrupted keys to be used or secrets to leak. The fault_err_req mechanism may trigger security escalation; a stuck-high request could cause denial of service or block secure recovery. The op_done interrupt signals completion of security-sensitive operations; a missed interrupt may stall or corrupt secure workflows.",
